    /// Window/session commands and view controls only. Prompt-execution
    /// choices live beside the prompt in the composer control row.
    fn render_toolbar(&self, cx: &mut Context<Self>) -> Toolbar {
        let this = cx.weak_entity();
        let items = vec![
            ToolbarItem::command("new-chat", "New Chat", CommandId::new(commands::SESSION_NEW))
                .priority(240),
            ToolbarItem::command("stop", "Stop", CommandId::new(commands::SESSION_INTERRUPT))
                .priority(250)
                .image(TemplateImage::Stop),
            ToolbarItem::flexible_space("toolbar-leading-space"),
            ToolbarItem::segmented(
                "workspace",
                "Workspace",
                vec![
                    ToolbarSegment::new("conversation", "Conversation"),
                    ToolbarSegment::new("changes", "Changes"),
                ],
                Some(if self.changes_open { "changes" } else { "conversation" }),
                move |id, window, cx| {
                    let changes = id.as_ref() == "changes";
                    let _ = this.update(cx, |view, cx| {
                        view.set_changes_visible(changes, window, cx);
                    });
                },
            )
            .priority(220),
            ToolbarItem::toggle("details", "Details", CommandId::new(commands::DETAILS))
                .toggle_help("Show compact transcript", "Show detailed transcript")
                .priority(180),
            ToolbarItem::flexible_space("toolbar-trailing-space"),
            ToolbarItem::toggle("sidebar", "Sidebar", CommandId::new(commands::SIDEBAR))
                .priority(230)
                .image(TemplateImage::Sidebar),
            ToolbarItem::toggle("inspector", "Inspector", CommandId::new(commands::INSPECTOR))
                .priority(200)
                .image(TemplateImage::Inspector),
            ToolbarItem::search("search", "Search", self.search_field.clone()),
        ];
        Toolbar::new("sandcat-toolbar", "Document", self.commands.clone(), items)
            .display_mode(ToolbarDisplayMode::IconOnly)
            .customizable(false)
    }
```

Wait — `ToolbarItem::segmented` `selected` param is `Option<impl Into<SharedString>>` — `Some(&str)` works. Good.

Issue: `ToolbarItem::toggle` returns Self; `.image()` works on Command kind. Good.

Potential issue: two flexible spaces in IconOnly mode — flexible space items have priority 255 and always visible; `fit_toolbar` handles widths. Fine.

`Toolbar::new` label: "Document" is a generic label; HIG toolbar accessibility label should describe toolbar. Since no explicit guidance in doc, maybe "Sandcat" or "Document". The doc doesn't specify. Hmm — "do not invent new UI" — a label is needed by API. I'll use "Document" (generic) as in Silvestris tests. Actually "Sandcat" more apt. But label isn't visible in IconOnly mode (used for accessibility/customization). Let me use "Document" to match standard toolbar naming in Silvestris tests. Hmm, better "Sandcat" for consumer identity? The doc doesn't specify. I'll use "Document" (neutral, from Silvestris example) — but "do not invent" — either is invented. I'll pick "Document" as it's the standard example.

Actually, we could use the window title? `self.window_title()` returns String. That would be dynamic, causing element identity? No, label isn't id. But dynamic label per session might be odd. Use "Document".

Let me write the replacement.

